// microbench hop1_knows: the distinct knows-neighbors of a person, both directions (T1).
// Reads: the knows edge index from the anchor (_from and _to sides); returns each neighbor's
// _key only (no neighbor property is read).
// Evaluator: queries/hop.py _hop1("knows", "both", "Person") -- read_neighbors + dedup,
// count-final (the harness counts the returned keys).
// mb2 lineage: MB25 (1-hop ANY; mb2 did not deduplicate).
FOR v IN 1..1 ANY CONCAT("Person/", @personId) knows
    OPTIONS {order: "bfs", uniqueVertices: "global"}
    RETURN v._key
